    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "3Jhjj",
      "x": 20695,
      "y": 4802,
      "name": "note",
      "width": 250,
      "height": 80,
      "content": "Archive action added to history row hover actions (edit, archive, delete). "
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "YPGHd",
      "x": 30374,
      "y": 4566,
      "name": "note",
      "width": 280,
      "height": 180,
      "content": "Why does a user see the 'Archived' badge?\n\nWhen a user archives a conversation, it disappears from the sidebar to reduce clutter. However, if they later search for it, the conversation still appears in results. The 'Archived' badge tells the user this conversation is no longer in their active sidebar — so they understand why they can't find it there. Clicking the result should still open the conversation normally."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "GwmxI",
      "x": 36862,
      "y": 4669,
      "name": "note",
      "width": 300,
      "height": 130,
      "content": "Archived chat state: When a user opens an archived conversation (e.g. from search results), the chat input is replaced with an archived banner showing an archive icon, 'This conversation was archived' text, and an 'Unarchive' button. The conversation content remains fully readable. Clicking 'Unarchive' restores the chat input and returns the conversation to the sidebar."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "p4kf8",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 280,
      "name": "note1",
      "width": 300,
      "height": 80,
      "content": "Active/focus state: use $border-focus variable for stroke. Never hardcode #056CFF or #5098FF."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "7A3uA",
      "x": 18834,
      "y": 4803,
      "name": "Note - Save Icon",
      "width": 260,
      "height": 220,
      "content": "Save Icon\n\nThe save button appears in two places:\n• On the user's message — to save a prompt for reuse later\n• On the AI's response — to bookmark a helpful answer\n\nRationale: This is the most natural moment of discovery. The user just got a response that worked well and wants to keep it. No hunting through settings."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "mdmU2",
      "x": 42258,
      "y": 4499,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 400,
      "content": "Dictation Flow\n\n1. User taps the microphone icon in the chat input bar to start voice dictation.\n\n2. The app begins capturing audio and transcribing speech to text in real-time. The transcribed text appears in the chat input field as the user speaks.\n\n3. While dictating, a 'Stop Submit dictation' button appears, giving the user two options:\n   • Stop — pauses dictation so the user can review/edit the text before sending.\n   • Submit dictation — immediately sends the transcribed text as a message.\n\n4. The user can also just keep speaking and the text will continue appending to the input field.\n\n5. If the user stops speaking for a few seconds, dictation auto-pauses and they can review before submitting.\n\n\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "qWvsI",
      "x": 45152,
      "y": 4320,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 420,
      "content": "Arena Mode Flow\n\n1. User selects 'Arena Mode' from the model selector in the chat input bar. This enables side-by-side model comparison.\n\n2. Two model slots appear in the input bar. The user picks which AI models to compare (e.g. Kimi K2.5 vs DeepSeek V3.2).\n\n3. User types their prompt and submits. The same prompt is sent to both models simultaneously.\n\n4. Responses appear in a split-view layout, showing each model's output side by side for direct comparison.\n\n5. After reviewing, the user can:\n   • Vote for the better response\n   • Regenerate with different models\n   • Save the comparison result\n\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "YZy4T",
      "x": 49330,
      "y": 4607,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 280,
      "content": "Save Icon\n\nThe save button appears in two places:\n• On the user's message — to save a prompt for reuse later\n• On the AI's response — to bookmark a helpful answer\n\nRationale: This is the most natural moment of discovery. The user just got a response that worked well and wants to keep it. No hunting through settings."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "tPjpb",
      "x": 51472,
      "y": 4307,
      "name": "Save Flow Note",
      "width": 300,
      "height": 220,
      "content": "Save Flow:\n\nWhen the user taps the save icon on the AI response action bar, a popover appears with save options:\n\n1. Save to My Prompts — saves the response directly\n2. Add to Collection — opens a sub-menu to pick a collection\n3. Create New Collection — creates a new collection\n\nAfter saving, a success toast confirms the action."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "HF6lV",
      "x": 50948,
      "y": 4383,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 420,
      "content": "Save Prompt Flow\n\n1. User taps the save icon on a message (user prompt or AI response).\n\n2. A modal appears with:\n   • The prompt/response text in an editable textarea so the user can refine the wording\n   • A Personal/Team toggle to choose where to save\n\n3. User taps 'Save Prompt' to confirm.\n\n4. A success toast appears: 'Saved to My Prompts'.\n\n5. Saved prompts are accessible from the Prompts Library.\n\nRationale: This is the most natural moment of discovery — the user just got a response that worked well and wants to keep it. No hunting through settings."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "Y2bwL",
      "x": 55657,
      "y": 4821,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 219,
      "content": "Users can also access saved prompts, prompt library from the side bar so it is easily accessible\n"
    },
